+section('agent-setup', 'Agent setup', 'terminal')
  p.
    The Agent (#[code thub]) is a stateless Node.js CLI. Install it wherever jobs are submitted from:
    a developer machine (macOS, Linux or Windows with Node.js 20+) or a CI runner.

  h3.h6 Install
  +code('Developer machine').
    npm i -g @andrian.yablonskyy/thub-agent
    thub --version
  p.small.
    In CI you don't need a global install: #[code npx -y @andrian.yablonskyy/thub-agent run …].

  h3.h6 Get your access key
  p.small.
    Every person has a user with one #[strong access key]. An admin creates you on #[a(href="/admin/users") Users]
    (or with #[code thub-admin user add]) and hands you the key, which is shown only once. Maintainers and admins can also
    create or replace their own on their #[a(href="/profile") profile]. Your #[strong role] decides what you can do:
  table.table.table-sm.small.w-auto
    thead
      tr
        th Role
        th Agent
        th Dashboard
    tbody
      tr
        td: strong User
        td submits jobs, sees and cancels only their own
        td no
      tr
        td: strong Maintainer
        td submits jobs, sees and cancels every job
        td yes, without Users, Settings and CI tokens
      tr
        td: strong Admin
        td like a Maintainer
        td everything
  p.small.
    Pipelines use a #[strong CI token] instead (#[a(href="/admin/agents") CI tokens], admins): their jobs get A- ids and they
    read every job. People's jobs get M- ids.

  h3.h6 Configure
  +code('Save the settings once').
    thub config set url   #{coordinatorUrl}
    thub config set key   thk_…
  p.small.
    These are saved in #[code ~/.config/thub/agent.json]. Which runner group your jobs run in isn't an Agent
    setting: an admin or maintainer sets it for your user on the dashboard (#[code thub whoami] shows it). Order of precedence: flags (#[code --url], #[code --key]) →
    environment → config file.
  table.table.table-sm.small
    thead
      tr
        th Variable
        th Meaning
    tbody
      tr
        td: code THUB_URL
        td Coordinator URL, e.g. #[code #{coordinatorUrl}]
      tr
        td: code THUB_KEY
        td Your access key, or a CI token in a pipeline. Keep it in your CI's secret store. (#[code THUB_TOKEN], #[code --token] and a saved #[code token] still work: the old names.)
      tr
        td: code THUB_NO_SELF_UPDATE=1
        td Don't install admin-requested Agent updates on this machine
  +code('Check the connection and your key').
    thub whoami             # jane (user) <jane@example.com>
    thub key show           # your key's last characters, created, last used
    thub key rotate         # replace it — the old one stops at once; saved to the config file if it came from there
    thub resources          # lists the Clients and their status
    thub jobs --mine        # your recent jobs
  p.small.mb-0.
    When an admin requests an Agent update, the next #[code thub] command installs it and then runs on
    the new version. If it can't install (e.g. no permission in CI), it prints the manual command and
    carries on with the current version.
